module

public import TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.Curves.StableReduction.Model.Basic
public import TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.Curves.StableReduction.NumericalType.Basic
public import TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IntersectionNumber.Weight
public import TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.SpecialFiber.Reduced

/-!
# The numerical type of a regular model

Let `R` be a local ring of dimension at most one whose maximal ideal is generated by a
nonzerodivisor `π`, for instance a discrete valuation ring with a uniformizer, with residue field
`k`, and let `X` be a regular Noetherian integral scheme, proper and flat over `R`, all of whose
points have codimension at most two, such as a proper regular model of a curve over `R`. Let
`Cᵢ` be the irreducible components of the special fibre, with their reduced structures, and
suppose that `H⁰` and `H¹` of the structure sheaf of every `Cᵢ` are finite-dimensional over `k`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.FiniteDimensionalComponentCohomology`).

When the special fibre is connected, the data

* the multiplicities `mᵢ` of the components in the special fibre
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberMultiplicity`),
* the weights `wᵢ = [κᵢ : k]` of their constant fields `κᵢ = H⁰(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberWeight`),
* the intersection matrix `aᵢⱼ = (Cⱼ · Cᵢ)`
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix`), and
* the genera `gᵢ = dim_{κᵢ} H¹(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})` of the components over their constant fields

form a numerical type in the sense of [Stacks, Tag 0C6Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C6Z),
the **numerical type of the regular model**
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType`). Its weighted Picard group
`TauCeti.NumericalType.Pic` and signed genus `TauCeti.NumericalType.arithmeticGenus` are the
combinatorial invariants through which the prime-to-residue-characteristic Picard torsion of the
generic fibre controls the special fibre in the proof of semistable reduction in genus at least
two ([Stacks, Tag 0CEI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CEI)).

Connectedness of the special fibre is a hypothesis here. It is exactly the connectedness axiom of
the numerical type
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.isPreconnected_preimage_closedPoint_iff_reflTransGen`), and over a
discrete valuation ring it holds for instance when the generic fibre is geometrically connected,
by Zariski's connectedness theorem. The genera are taken over the constant fields `κᵢ` rather than
over `k`, and are not the genera of the normalizations of the `Cᵢ`; over `k` they give
`dim_k H¹(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ}) = wᵢ gᵢ`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberWeight_mul_finrank_cohomology_one`), hence
`wᵢ (gᵢ - 1) = -χ_k(𝒪_{Cᵢ})` and the signed-genus identity
`g(T) = 1 - ∑ᵢ mᵢ χ_k(𝒪_{Cᵢ}) - (∑ᵢ mᵢ (Cᵢ · Cᵢ)) / 2`. Generator independence
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_congr`) yields a uniformizer-free
invariant `TauCeti.Model.numericalType` for proper regular integral models of relative dimension at
most one over a discrete valuation ring.

## Main declarations

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType` and `TauCeti.Model.numericalType`: the
  numerical type of the special fibre of a regular model, with its data described by
  `specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity`, `specialFiberNumericalType_weight`,
  `specialFiberNumericalType_intersection`, and `specialFiberNumericalType_genus` (and
  `TauCeti.Model` counterparts).
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_congr` and
  `TauCeti.Model.numericalType_eq_specialFiberNumericalType`: independence of the chosen generator
  of the maximal ideal.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_adj_iff` and
  `forall_specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity_eq_one_iff` (with `TauCeti.Model` counterparts):
  graph adjacency and reducedness of the scheme-theoretic special fibre.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_weight_mul_genus_sub_one` and
  `specialFiberNumericalType_arithmeticGenus_eq_sum_eulerCharBelow` (with `TauCeti.Model`
  counterparts): `wᵢ (gᵢ - 1) = -χ_k(𝒪_{Cᵢ})` and the total arithmetic-genus identity.

## References

* [The Stacks Project, Tag 0C6Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C6Z), for numerical types,
  [Section 55.9 (Tag 0C5Y)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C5Y), for the numerical type
  attached to a regular model, and
  [Lemma 55.9.9 (Tag 0C9U)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C9U).
* Q. Liu, *Algebraic Geometry and Arithmetic Curves*, Section 9.1.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry IsLocalRing Order
open TauCeti TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
open AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData (vanishingIdeal)
open AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules (eulerCharBelow eulerCharBelow_two)

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [Ring.DimensionLEOne R]
  {X : Scheme.{u}} (toBase : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) [IsIntegral X] [IsNoetherian X]
  [TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegular X] [IsProper toBase] [Flat toBase]
  (hX : ∀ x : X, coheight x ≤ 2) (hη : toBase (genericPoint X) ≠ closedPoint R)
  (h₀ : toBase.FiniteDimensionalComponentCohomology 0)
  (h₁ : toBase.FiniteDimensionalComponentCohomology 1)
  {π : R} (hπ : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π}) (hreg : IsSMulRegular R π)
  (hconn : _root_.IsPreconnected (toBase ⁻¹' {closedPoint R}))

/-- **The numerical type of a regular model.** Let `X` be a regular Noetherian integral scheme,
proper and flat over a local ring `R` of dimension at most one whose maximal ideal is generated by
a nonzerodivisor `π`, with all points of codimension at most two and generic point away from the
closed point. Suppose that `H⁰` and `H¹` of the structure sheaf of every component `Cᵢ` of the
special fibre are finite-dimensional over the residue field `k`, and that the special fibre is
connected. Its numerical type ([Stacks, Tag 0C6Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C6Z)) has
the components of the special fibre as its components, with

* multiplicity `mᵢ` the multiplicity of `Cᵢ` in the divisor of `π`,
* weight `wᵢ = [κᵢ : k]` the degree of the constant field `κᵢ = H⁰(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`,
* intersection matrix `aᵢⱼ = (Cⱼ · Cᵢ)`, and
* genus `gᵢ = dim_{κᵢ} H¹(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`, the arithmetic genus of `Cᵢ` over its constant field.

The definition is exposed so that the component type is the finite set of codimension-one points
of the special fibre indexing `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix`. -/
@[expose]
def specialFiberNumericalType : NumericalType.{u} where
  Component := (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
    (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset
  componentDecidableEq := Classical.decEq _
  componentNonempty := by
    obtain ⟨η, hc⟩ := toBase.exists_codimensionOnePoint_base_eq_closedPoint hη
    exact ⟨⟨η, (Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mpr hc⟩⟩
  multiplicity j := ⟨toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π j,
    toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity_pos hη (hπ ▸ Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self π)
      (toBase.ne_zero_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη hπ) j ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp j.2)⟩
  weight i := ⟨toBase.specialFiberWeight ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2),
    toBase.specialFiberWeight_pos _ (h₀ i ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2))⟩
  intersection := toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη
  intersection_isSymm := toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_isSymm hX hη h₀ h₁
  offDiagonal_nonneg _ _ := toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_nonneg_of_ne hX hη h₀ h₁
  connected := toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_reflTransGen hX hη h₀ h₁ hconn
  fiber_relation i := by
    have h := congrFun
      (toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_mulVec_specialFiberMultiplicity hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg) i
    simpa [Matrix.mulVec, dotProduct, mul_comm] using h
  weight_dvd := toBase.specialFiberWeight_dvd_specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη
  genus i := Module.finrank
    Γ((vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {((i : CodimensionOnePoint X) : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme, ⊤)
    (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial (vanishingIdeal
      ⟨closure {((i : CodimensionOnePoint X) : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1)

/-- The component index type of `specialFiberNumericalType` is the finite set of codimension-one
points of `X` lying over the closed point. -/
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_component :
    (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).Component =
      (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
        (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset :=
  rfl

/-- A codimension-one point of `X` arises as a component of `specialFiberNumericalType` if and only
if it maps to `closedPoint R`. -/
theorem exists_specialFiberNumericalType_component_iff (x : CodimensionOnePoint X) :
    (∃ i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).Component, i.1 = x) ↔
      toBase x = closedPoint R :=
  ⟨by rintro ⟨i, rfl⟩; exact (Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2,
    fun hx ↦ ⟨⟨x, (Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mpr hx⟩, rfl⟩⟩

/-- Every component of `specialFiberNumericalType` maps to `closedPoint R`. -/
theorem base_specialFiberNumericalType_component
    (i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).Component) :
    toBase i.1 = closedPoint R :=
  (Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2

/-- The multiplicity of a component of the numerical type of a regular model is its multiplicity
in the divisor of `π`. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity
    (i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).Component) :
    ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).multiplicity i : ℕ) =
      toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π i.1 :=
  rfl

/-- The weight of a component of the numerical type of a regular model is the degree
`dim_k H⁰(C, 𝒪_C)` of its constant field over the residue field. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_weight
    (i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).Component) :
    ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).weight i : ℕ) =
      toBase.specialFiberWeight
        (toBase.base_specialFiberNumericalType_component hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn i) :=
  rfl

/-- The intersection matrix of the numerical type of a regular model is the intersection matrix
of its special fibre. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_intersection :
    (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).intersection =
      toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη :=
  rfl

/-- The genus of a component `C` of the numerical type of a regular model is
`dim_{κ_C} H¹(C, 𝒪_C)`, over the ring `κ_C = H⁰(C, 𝒪_C)` of global functions on `C`, which is its
constant field. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_genus
    (i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).Component) :
    (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).genus i = Module.finrank
      Γ((vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme, ⊤)
      (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
        (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1) :=
  rfl

/-- Two components are adjacent in `specialFiberNumericalType` if and only if they are distinct and
their closures in `X` meet. -/
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_adj_iff
    (i j : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).Component) :
    (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).Adj i j ↔
      i ≠ j ∧ (closure {(i.1 : X)} ∩ closure {(j.1 : X)}).Nonempty := by
  rw [NumericalType.adj_iff, specialFiberNumericalType_intersection]
  exact and_congr_right fun hij ↦ toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_pos_iff hX hη h₀ h₁ hij

/-- **Generator independence of the special-fibre numerical type.** Any two nonzerodivisor
generators of `maximalIdeal R` define the same `NumericalType`. -/
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_congr {π' : R} (hπ' : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π'})
    (hreg' : IsSMulRegular R π') :
    toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn =
      toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ' hreg' hconn :=
  let T := toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn
  let T' := toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ' hreg' hconn
  T.reindex_refl.symm.trans (T.reindex_eq (T' := T') (.refl _) (fun i ↦ Subtype.ext
    (toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity_eq_of_span_eq (hπ'.symm.trans hπ) i.1))
    (fun _ ↦ rfl) (fun _ _ ↦ rfl) fun _ ↦ rfl)

/-- Every component of `specialFiberNumericalType` has multiplicity one if and only if the
scheme-theoretic special fibre is reduced. -/
theorem forall_specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity_eq_one_iff :
    (∀ i, (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).multiplicity i = 1) ↔
      IsReduced (specialFiber R toBase).left := by
  rw [toBase.isReduced_specialFiber_iff_specialFiberMultiplicity_eq_one_of_isRegular hX hη hπ]
  refine ⟨fun h x hx ↦ ?_, fun h i ↦ PNat.coe_eq_one_iff.mp
    (h i.1 (toBase.base_specialFiberNumericalType_component hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn i))⟩
  obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ :=
    (toBase.exists_specialFiberNumericalType_component_iff hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn x).mpr hx
  exact PNat.coe_eq_one_iff.mpr (h i)

/-- For each component `Cᵢ` of the special fibre, `wᵢ gᵢ = dim_k H¹(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`. -/
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_weight_mul_genus
    (i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).Component) :
    letI := subschemeOverResidueField (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
      (toBase.base_specialFiberNumericalType_component hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn i))
    ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).weight i : ℕ) *
        (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).genus i =
      Module.finrank (ResidueField R) (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
        (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1) := by
  rw [specialFiberNumericalType_weight, specialFiberNumericalType_genus]
  exact toBase.specialFiberWeight_mul_finrank_cohomology_one
    (toBase.base_specialFiberNumericalType_component hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn i)

/-- For each component `Cᵢ` of the special fibre, `wᵢ (gᵢ - 1) = -χ_k(𝒪_{Cᵢ})`, where `χ_k` is the
degree-`2` truncated Euler characteristic `dim_k H⁰ - dim_k H¹` over the residue field. -/
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_weight_mul_genus_sub_one
    (i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).Component) :
    letI := subschemeOverResidueField (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
      (toBase.base_specialFiberNumericalType_component hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn i))
    ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).weight i : ℤ) *
        (((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).genus i : ℤ) - 1) =
      -eulerCharBelow (ResidueField R)
        (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
          (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 2 := by
  have hi := toBase.base_specialFiberNumericalType_component hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn i
  let := subschemeOverResidueField (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton hi)
  have hwg : ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).weight i : ℤ) *
      ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).genus i : ℤ) =
    (Module.finrank (ResidueField R) (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
      (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1) : ℤ) := by
    exact_mod_cast toBase.specialFiberNumericalType_weight_mul_genus hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn i
  have hw0 : ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).weight i : ℤ) =
      (Module.finrank (ResidueField R) (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
        (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 0) : ℤ) := by
    rw [specialFiberNumericalType_weight, specialFiberWeight_def]
  rw [eulerCharBelow_two, mul_sub, mul_one, hwg, hw0]; ring

/-- Weighted sum of `mᵢ wᵢ (gᵢ - 1)` across `specialFiberNumericalType`, equal to
`-∑ᵢ mᵢ χ_k(𝒪_{Cᵢ})`. -/
theorem sum_specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity_mul_weight_mul_genus_sub_one :
    ∑ i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).Component,
        ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).multiplicity i : ℤ) *
          ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).weight i : ℤ) *
          (((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).genus i : ℤ) - 1) =
      -∑ i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).Component,
        ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).multiplicity i : ℤ) *
          (letI := subschemeOverResidueField
            (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
              (toBase.base_specialFiberNumericalType_component hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn i))
          eulerCharBelow (ResidueField R)
            (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme
            (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
              (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 2) := by
  rw [← Finset.sum_neg_distrib]; refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_
  rw [mul_assoc,
    toBase.specialFiberNumericalType_weight_mul_genus_sub_one hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn i, mul_neg]

/-- Signed genus of `specialFiberNumericalType` in terms of `χ_k(𝒪_{Cᵢ})` and self-intersections:
`g(T) = 1 - ∑ᵢ mᵢ χ_k(𝒪_{Cᵢ}) - (∑ᵢ mᵢ (Cᵢ · Cᵢ)) / 2`. -/
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_arithmeticGenus_eq_sum_eulerCharBelow :
    (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).arithmeticGenus =
      1 - (∑ i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).Component,
          ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).multiplicity i : ℤ) *
            (letI := subschemeOverResidueField
              (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
                (toBase.base_specialFiberNumericalType_component hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn i))
            eulerCharBelow (ResidueField R)
              (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme
              (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
                (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 2)) -
        (∑ i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).Component,
          ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).multiplicity i : ℤ) *
            toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη i i) / 2 := by
  rw [NumericalType.arithmeticGenus_def,
    toBase.sum_specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity_mul_weight_mul_genus_sub_one
      hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn]
  simp only [specialFiberNumericalType_intersection]; ring

/-- Division-free form of `specialFiberNumericalType_arithmeticGenus_eq_sum_eulerCharBelow`:
`2 g(T) = 2 - 2 ∑ᵢ mᵢ χ_k(𝒪_{Cᵢ}) - ∑ᵢ mᵢ (Cᵢ · Cᵢ)`. -/
theorem two_mul_specialFiberNumericalType_arithmeticGenus_eq_sum_eulerCharBelow :
    2 * (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).arithmeticGenus =
      2 - 2 * (∑ i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).Component,
          ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).multiplicity i : ℤ) *
            (letI := subschemeOverResidueField
              (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
                (toBase.base_specialFiberNumericalType_component hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn i))
            eulerCharBelow (ResidueField R)
              (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme
              (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
                (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 2)) -
        ∑ i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).Component,
          ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).multiplicity i : ℤ) *
            toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη i i := by
  rw [NumericalType.two_mul_arithmeticGenus,
    toBase.sum_specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity_mul_weight_mul_genus_sub_one
      hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn]
  simp only [specialFiberNumericalType_intersection]; ring

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

namespace TauCeti.Model

variable {R K : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsDiscreteValuationRing R]
  [Field K] [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K] {C : Scheme.{u}} {toK : C ⟶ Spec (.of K)}

/-- **The numerical type of a proper regular model.** For a proper integral regular model `M` of
relative dimension at most one over a discrete valuation ring `R`, with connected special fibre and
finite-dimensional `H⁰` and `H¹` on the reduced irreducible components of the special fibre, this
is the uniformizer-independent `TauCeti.NumericalType` of the special fibre. Both `[M.IsProper]`
and `[RelativeDimensionLE 1 M.toBase]` are synthesized automatically whenever
`[FamilyOfCurves M.toBase]` is in scope. -/
@[expose] def numericalType (M : Model R K C toK) [M.IsProper] [RelativeDimensionLE 1 M.toBase]
    [IsIntegral M.total] [TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegular M.total]
    (h₀ : M.toBase.FiniteDimensionalComponentCohomology 0)
    (h₁ : M.toBase.FiniteDimensionalComponentCohomology 1)
    (hconn : _root_.IsPreconnected (M.toBase ⁻¹' {closedPoint R})) : NumericalType.{u} :=
  M.toBase.specialFiberNumericalType M.toBase.coheight_le_succ_of_relativeDimensionLE
    (M.toBase.base_genericPoint_ne_closedPoint (IsDiscreteValuationRing.not_a_field R))
    h₀ h₁
    (IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_irreducible R).choose_spec.maximalIdeal_eq
    (mul_right_injective₀ (IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_irreducible R).choose_spec.ne_zero)
    hconn

section ModelAPI

variable (M : Model R K C toK) [M.IsProper] [RelativeDimensionLE 1 M.toBase] [IsIntegral M.total]
  [TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegular M.total]
  (h₀ : M.toBase.FiniteDimensionalComponentCohomology 0)
  (h₁ : M.toBase.FiniteDimensionalComponentCohomology 1)
  (hconn : _root_.IsPreconnected (M.toBase ⁻¹' {closedPoint R}))

/-- A codimension-one point of `M.total` arises as a component of `M.numericalType` if and only if
it maps to `closedPoint R`. -/
theorem exists_numericalType_component_iff (x : CodimensionOnePoint M.total) :
    (∃ i : (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Component, i.1 = x) ↔ M.toBase x = closedPoint R :=
  M.toBase.exists_specialFiberNumericalType_component_iff _ _ h₀ h₁ _ _ hconn x

/-- Every component of `M.numericalType` maps to `closedPoint R`. -/
theorem base_numericalType_component (i : (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    M.toBase i.1 = closedPoint R :=
  M.toBase.base_specialFiberNumericalType_component _ _ h₀ h₁ _ _ hconn i

/-- For any generator `π` of `maximalIdeal R`, the multiplicity of `i` in `M.numericalType` is
`M.toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π i.1`. -/
theorem numericalType_multiplicity {π : R} (hπ : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π})
    (i : (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    ((M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).multiplicity i : ℕ) =
      M.toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π i.1 :=
  M.toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity_eq_of_span_eq
    ((IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_irreducible R).choose_spec.maximalIdeal_eq.symm.trans hπ) i.1

/-- The weight of a component in `M.numericalType` is `dim_k H⁰(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`. -/
@[simp] theorem numericalType_weight (i : (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    ((M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).weight i : ℕ) =
      M.toBase.specialFiberWeight (M.base_numericalType_component h₀ h₁ hconn i) :=
  rfl

/-- The intersection matrix of `M.numericalType` is the special-fibre intersection matrix. -/
@[simp] theorem numericalType_intersection :
    (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).intersection =
      M.toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix M.toBase.coheight_le_succ_of_relativeDimensionLE
        (M.toBase.base_genericPoint_ne_closedPoint (IsDiscreteValuationRing.not_a_field R)) :=
  rfl

/-- The genus of a component in `M.numericalType` is `dim_{κᵢ} H¹(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})` over `κᵢ`. -/
@[simp] theorem numericalType_genus (i : (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).genus i =
      Module.finrank Γ((vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : M.total)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme, ⊤)
        (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
          (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : M.total)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1) :=
  rfl

/-- Two components of `M.numericalType` are adjacent iff they are distinct and their closures in
`M.total` meet. -/
theorem numericalType_adj_iff (i j : (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Adj i j ↔
      i ≠ j ∧ (closure {(i.1 : M.total)} ∩ closure {(j.1 : M.total)}).Nonempty :=
  M.toBase.specialFiberNumericalType_adj_iff _ _ h₀ h₁ _ _ hconn i j

/-- For any generator `π` of `maximalIdeal R`, `M.numericalType` equals
`M.toBase.specialFiberNumericalType`. -/
theorem numericalType_eq_specialFiberNumericalType (hX : ∀ x : M.total, coheight x ≤ 2)
    (hη : M.toBase (genericPoint M.total) ≠ closedPoint R) {π : R}
    (hπ : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π}) (hreg : IsSMulRegular R π) :
    M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn =
      M.toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn :=
  M.toBase.specialFiberNumericalType_congr _ _ h₀ h₁ _ _ hconn hπ hreg

/-- Every component of `M.numericalType` has multiplicity one iff the scheme-theoretic special fibre
of `M` is reduced. -/
theorem forall_numericalType_multiplicity_eq_one_iff :
    (∀ i, (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).multiplicity i = 1) ↔
      IsReduced (specialFiber R M.toBase).left :=
  M.toBase.forall_specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity_eq_one_iff _ _ h₀ h₁ _ _ hconn

/-- For each component `Cᵢ` of `M.numericalType`, `wᵢ gᵢ = dim_k H¹(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`. -/
theorem numericalType_weight_mul_genus (i : (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    letI := subschemeOverResidueField <|
      M.toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
        (M.base_numericalType_component h₀ h₁ hconn i)
    ((M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).weight i : ℕ) * (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).genus i =
      Module.finrank (ResidueField R) (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
        (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : M.total)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1) :=
  M.toBase.specialFiberNumericalType_weight_mul_genus _ _ h₀ h₁ _ _ hconn i

/-- For each component `Cᵢ` of `M.numericalType`, `wᵢ (gᵢ - 1) = -χ_k(𝒪_{Cᵢ})`. -/
theorem numericalType_weight_mul_genus_sub_one (i : (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    letI := subschemeOverResidueField <|
      M.toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
        (M.base_numericalType_component h₀ h₁ hconn i)
    ((M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).weight i : ℤ) *
        (((M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).genus i : ℤ) - 1) =
      -eulerCharBelow (ResidueField R)
        (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : M.total)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme
        (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
          (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : M.total)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 2 :=
  M.toBase.specialFiberNumericalType_weight_mul_genus_sub_one _ _ h₀ h₁ _ _ hconn i

/-- Weighted sum of `mᵢ wᵢ (gᵢ - 1)` across `M.numericalType`, equal to `-∑ᵢ mᵢ χ_k(𝒪_{Cᵢ})`. -/
theorem sum_numericalType_multiplicity_mul_weight_mul_genus_sub_one :
    ∑ i : (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Component,
        ((M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).multiplicity i : ℤ) *
          ((M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).weight i : ℤ) *
          (((M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).genus i : ℤ) - 1) =
      -∑ i : (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Component,
        ((M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).multiplicity i : ℤ) *
          (letI := subschemeOverResidueField <|
            M.toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
              (M.base_numericalType_component h₀ h₁ hconn i)
          eulerCharBelow (ResidueField R)
            (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : M.total)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme
            (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
              (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : M.total)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 2) :=
  M.toBase.sum_specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity_mul_weight_mul_genus_sub_one _ _ h₀ h₁ _ _
    hconn

/-- The signed genus of `M.numericalType` in terms of `χ_k(𝒪_{Cᵢ})` and self-intersections. -/
theorem numericalType_arithmeticGenus_eq_sum_eulerCharBelow :
    (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).arithmeticGenus =
      1 - (∑ i : (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Component,
          ((M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).multiplicity i : ℤ) *
            (letI := subschemeOverResidueField <|
              M.toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
                (M.base_numericalType_component h₀ h₁ hconn i)
            eulerCharBelow (ResidueField R)
              (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : M.total)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme
              (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
                (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : M.total)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 2)) -
        (∑ i : (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Component,
          ((M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).multiplicity i : ℤ) *
            (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).intersection i i) / 2 :=
  M.toBase.specialFiberNumericalType_arithmeticGenus_eq_sum_eulerCharBelow _ _ h₀ h₁ _ _ hconn

/-- Division-free form of `Model.numericalType_arithmeticGenus_eq_sum_eulerCharBelow`:
`2 g(T) = 2 - 2 ∑ᵢ mᵢ χ_k(𝒪_{Cᵢ}) - ∑ᵢ mᵢ (Cᵢ · Cᵢ)`. -/
theorem two_mul_numericalType_arithmeticGenus_eq_sum_eulerCharBelow :
    2 * (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).arithmeticGenus =
      2 - 2 * (∑ i : (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Component,
          ((M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).multiplicity i : ℤ) *
            (letI := subschemeOverResidueField <|
              M.toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
                (M.base_numericalType_component h₀ h₁ hconn i)
            eulerCharBelow (ResidueField R)
              (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : M.total)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme
              (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
                (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : M.total)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 2)) -
        ∑ i : (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Component,
          ((M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).multiplicity i : ℤ) *
            (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).intersection i i :=
  M.toBase.two_mul_specialFiberNumericalType_arithmeticGenus_eq_sum_eulerCharBelow _ _ h₀ h₁ _ _
    hconn

end ModelAPI

